 "short_description": "A slow-twitch, oxidative skeletal muscle fibre built for endurance: a single unbranched, cylindrical cell running centimetres long (~40-60 um across), with hundreds of nuclei flattened at the PERIPHERY just under the sarcolemma, regular cross-striations (A/I bands, Z-disc to Z-disc sarcomeres), and dense mitochondria and myoglobin giving it a deep red colour and an essentially inexhaustible aerobic ATP supply. Fed by a rich capillary bed and driven by a small, easily-excited motor neuron, it is recruited first for almost any movement and dominates postural muscle such as the soleus.",
